Added characterization
- Reusable twin-target harness with native Target-A active and mesh Target-B represented as an explicit pending seam.
- Scenario/phase oracle records input, resolution, stdout, stderr, exit, typed-outcome projection, receipts, durable state, terminal input, and reconciliation.
- Zero-mutation assertions cover read-only, dry-run, and pre-admission refusal phases in the reusable oracle.
- Accepted success requires exactly one independently observed non-empty terminal input.
- Post-effect failure retains the observed effect and requires explicit reconciliation without blind replay.
- Real local-tmux fixture observes missing-registration refusal and exact signed input delivery, including literal escape and UTF-8 bytes.
- Real local-native fixture starts through setsid with closed stdin, verifies no controlling terminal on the actuator host, and verifies an explicit PTY master/slave pair for the child.
- Real local-native drive observes exact signed UTF-8 input and one carriage return, raw mode, a 101x37 TIOCSWINSZ resize, partial writes, closed-pipe failure, and oversized/control-bearing input failure without terminal mutation.
- Escape-sequence chunking and split UTF-8 decoding are characterized independently.

